    "['ipv6 unicast-routing', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set routing-options rib inet6.0 static multipath', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set routing-options rib inet6.0 static multipath', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset routing-options rib inet6.0 static multipath\\n##\\n\\nOr alternatively, if you prefer the more direct equivalent:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols router-advertisement interface all\\n##\\n\\nNote: Juniper doesn\\'t have an exact 1:1 equivalent to Cisco\\'s \"ipv6 unicast-routing\" since IPv6 routing is always enabled in Junos. The first option creates the IPv6 routing table, while the second enables router advertisements which implies IPv6 routing functionality. Choose based on your specific needs.', 'trans_template': 'set routing-options rib inet6.0 static multipath'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols router-advertisement interface all', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set protocols router-advertisement interface all', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset routing-options rib inet6.0 static multipath\\n##\\n\\nOr alternatively, if you prefer the more direct equivalent:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols router-advertisement interface all\\n##\\n\\nNote: Juniper doesn\\'t have an exact 1:1 equivalent to Cisco\\'s \"ipv6 unicast-routing\" since IPv6 routing is always enabled in Junos. The first option creates the IPv6 routing table, while the second enables router advertisements which implies IPv6 routing functionality. Choose based on your specific needs.', 'trans_template': 'set protocols router-advertisement interface all'}]]": 1,
