    "['no shutdown', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/0 disable false', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 disable false\\n##\\n\\nFor Juniper devices, the equivalent of Cisco\\'s \"no shutdown\" is \"disable false\" in the interface configuration context. This command enables the interface (removes the shutdown state).\\n\\nNote: The command is specific to the interface GigabitEthernet1/0/0 from your example. For other interfaces, you would replace \"ge-1/0/0\" with the appropriate interface name (e.g., \"ge-1/0/1\" or \"ge-1/0/2\").', 'trans_template': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/0 disable false'}]]": 1,
    "['ipv6 enable', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet6', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet6\\n##\\n\\nFor Juniper devices, the equivalent of Cisco's `ipv6 enable` command is to configure the interface with `family inet6` (IPv6 protocol family). Note that in Juniper, you typically specify the logical unit (usually unit 0) when configuring interfaces.\", 'trans_template': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet6'}]]": 1,
    "['ipv6 address [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet6 address 2001:DB8:3::2/64', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco `ipv6 address` command:\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet6 address 2001:DB8:3::2/64\\n##\\n\\nThe translation notes:\\n1. Juniper uses `ge-1/0/0` instead of Cisco's `GigabitEthernet1/0/0`\\n2. Juniper requires specification of a logical unit (typically unit 0)\\n3. The address family is specified as `family inet6`\\n4. The IPv6 address format remains the same\", 'trans_template': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet6 address 2001:DB8:3::2/64'}]]": 1,
