    "['ipv6 enable', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces <interface-name> family inet6', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset interfaces <interface-name> family inet6\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, you would replace `<interface-name>` with the actual interface name (e.g., `ge-1/0/0`). The `family inet6` enables IPv6 on the interface, which is equivalent to Cisco's `ipv6 enable` command. The interface name format in Juniper typically uses hyphens (e.g., `ge-1/0/0` instead of `GigabitEthernet1/0/0`).\", 'trans_template': 'set interfaces <interface-name> family inet6'}]]": 1,
